title: _request sanitises header values but not header names
updated: 2026-08-24T04:21:03Z
---

The headers option strips CR/LF from each value but passes the key through untouched, so a caller-supplied header name containing CR/LF can inject an extra header line. Not currently reachable -- the only caller is the fixed literal X-Registry-Auth in Images.pm -- but the sanitiser is incomplete and the option is public. Strip or reject CR/LF in the name the same way, and cover it in t/role_http.t alongside the existing value case. Found while writing that file (ticket 2).
